# Source Cook time: 40 min
# Source Servings: 2-4
# Conversion note: 600ml (1 Pint); prep time excludes 3-4 hours rise and cooling. Pint locale and rounding are unresolved; prep time is not active or total time.

::ingredients

(water, warm) 600ml / 1 Pint
(active dry yeast) 1tbsp
(honey) 7tbsp
(flour) 1.5kg
(egg) 3
(salt) 1tbsp
(poppy seeds) 1tbsp
(olive oil) 4tbsp

::equipment

(bowl, large)
(baking tray) 2
(oven)
(cooling rack)

::instructions

(water) <pour, large bowl>
    + (active dry yeast) <sprinkle>
{wet} = (honey) + (olive oil) + (egg) 2 + (salt)
{wet} <whisk>
{dough} = (water) + (active dry yeast) + {wet} + (flour)
{dough} <beat, or whisk, adding flour in small amounts>
    <knead, once viscous, until smooth and elastic and not sticky>
    <cover, damp cloth>
    <prove, 1-2h or until doubled>
    <place, floured chopping board>
    <divide, half>
Repeat [
    {half dough} <knead, adding flour as needed to prevent sticking>
        <divide, thirds>
        <roll, long snakes ~4cm / 1.5in in girth>
    {three snakes} <pinch, ends firmly>
        <plait>
]
for each half
(baking tray) <grease, or line with baking paper>
{plaits} <place, trays>
    <cover, dry cloth>
    <prove, 1h>
(oven) <preheat, 190c / Gas mark 5>
(egg) rest of <whisk>
{plaits} + (egg) rest of <brush>
    + (poppy seeds) <sprinkle>
    <bake, until hollow when tapped>
    <cool, rack, 1h before slicing>

::story

A kind of braided bread preparation.

